From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(approvals): expose effective scope and durable-grant ceiling

Approval consumers need an explicit, canonical scope so they can distinguish a
one-operation decision from a session grant or a durable grant without
parsing prompt text. Report that effective scope for fresh, cached, bypass,
and non-interactive approvals.

Thread an allow_permanent capability through the shared gate. Callers that do
not permit durable grants ignore permanent cache entries, retain eligible
session grants, and attenuate legacy CLI callback choices before persistence.
Gateway choices are normalized at the authority boundary; unknown choices and
unavailable permanent choices fail closed without changing approval state.

Keep native rendering and command/execute-code guard policy unchanged. The
implementation is intentionally shaped as two reusable upstream changes:
first canonical effective-scope metadata, then the durable-grant ceiling that
protects callers with narrower authority.

